  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2018-17-571",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "1afaf600dd2608f30f4fcb02b7bdcc9d7e90a9175743ea9a42338f6558262211",
      "evidence_id": "ev-1afaf600dd26-0000-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 2,
        "start": 2
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "APPEARANCES:\nAARON M. PANNER, ESQ., Washington, D.C.; on behalf of the Petitioner.\nPETER K. STRIS, ESQ., Los Angeles, California; on behalf of the Respondents.\nJONATHAN Y. ELLIS, Assistant to the Solicitor General, Department of Justice, Washington, D.C.; for the United States, as amicus curiae, supporting the Respondents."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Fourth Estate Public Benefit Corporation",
      "case_id": "2018-17-571",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "1afaf600dd2608f30f4fcb02b7bdcc9d7e90a9175743ea9a42338f6558262211",
      "evidence_id": "ev-1afaf600dd26-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. PANNER: Mr. Chief Justice, may it please the Court:\nThe Copyright Act provides strong textual evidence that the phrase \"registration has been made\" in Section 411(a) refers to the copyright owner's compliance with the registration requirement of Section 408(a). That reading is confirmed by the legislative history, the statute overruled cases that made the Register a gatekeeper to the courthouse, and the policy of the statute, which grants exclusive rights upon fixation of an original work, not by virtue of any administrative action.\nAnd as a matter of ordinary language, and in the Copyright Act's lexicon,"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2018-17-571",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "1afaf600dd2608f30f4fcb02b7bdcc9d7e90a9175743ea9a42338f6558262211",
      "evidence_id": "ev-1afaf600dd26-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 8,
        "start": 8
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: Do you drive without a driver's license when yours has expired because you wrote in to the registry of motor vehicles but they haven't yet licensed you?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2018-17-571",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "1afaf600dd2608f30f4fcb02b7bdcc9d7e90a9175743ea9a42338f6558262211",
      "evidence_id": "ev-1afaf600dd26-0000-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 11,
        "start": 11
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: Could you tell me as a matter of fact when is the copyright registration published?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Fourth Estate Public Benefit Corporation",
      "case_id": "2018-17-571",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "1afaf600dd2608f30f4fcb02b7bdcc9d7e90a9175743ea9a42338f6558262211",
      "evidence_id": "ev-1afaf600dd26-0000-0007",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 14,
        "start": 14
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. PANNER: The copyright claim, yes, Your Honor. That's what Section 410(d) says. Section 410(d) says the effective date of registration is the date on which the required application, deposit, and fee have been received in a form acceptable for registration."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2018-17-571",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "1afaf600dd2608f30f4fcb02b7bdcc9d7e90a9175743ea9a42338f6558262211",
      "evidence_id": "ev-1afaf600dd26-0000-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 17,
        "start": 17
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: Mr. Panner, I -- I -- I understand some of the policy arguments that you have on your side, but, I mean, the question is whether the text can -- can -- can be looked at that way."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2018-17-571",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "1afaf600dd2608f30f4fcb02b7bdcc9d7e90a9175743ea9a42338f6558262211",
      "evidence_id": "ev-1afaf600dd26-0000-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 17,
        "start": 17
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAVANAUGH: Mr. Panner, describe --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Fourth Estate Public Benefit Corporation",
      "case_id": "2018-17-571",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "1afaf600dd2608f30f4fcb02b7bdcc9d7e90a9175743ea9a42338f6558262211",
      "evidence_id": "ev-1afaf600dd26-0000-0008",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 18,
        "start": 18
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. PANNER: Well, Your Honor, obviously, we don't agree with that. And -- and let me try to say why I think, again, getting back to the textual evidence from the statute, the -- the issue is not granted or refused, and -- the issue is whether registration is made by the copyright owner."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Fourth Estate Public Benefit Corporation",
      "case_id": "2018-17-571",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "1afaf600dd2608f30f4fcb02b7bdcc9d7e90a9175743ea9a42338f6558262211",
      "evidence_id": "ev-1afaf600dd26-0000-0009",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "this is distinguishing a situation where registration has been made and it is or going to be granted because the Register agrees. But this is a situation in which the -- the registrar, notwithstanding the compliance with Section 408(a), has refused it."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2018-17-571",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "1afaf600dd2608f30f4fcb02b7bdcc9d7e90a9175743ea9a42338f6558262211",
      "evidence_id": "ev-1afaf600dd26-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 23,
        "start": 23
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: What do they do about the registrar not acting? Can final judgment be entered before the registrar acts?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2018-17-571",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "1afaf600dd2608f30f4fcb02b7bdcc9d7e90a9175743ea9a42338f6558262211",
      "evidence_id": "ev-1afaf600dd26-0001-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 26,
        "start": 26
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAVANAUGH: What are the practical problems? I think the message of your argument is, if you really understood how this works in the real world, we would agree with your reading. And -- and you're saying practical problems. I want to hear the practical problems."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2018-17-571",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "1afaf600dd2608f30f4fcb02b7bdcc9d7e90a9175743ea9a42338f6558262211",
      "evidence_id": "ev-1afaf600dd26-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 26,
        "start": 26
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAVANAUGH: And what are the -- what are the most -- what are the most severe practical problems? Delay, I understand."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2018-17-571",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "1afaf600dd2608f30f4fcb02b7bdcc9d7e90a9175743ea9a42338f6558262211",
      "evidence_id": "ev-1afaf600dd26-0001-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 28,
        "start": 28
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: How -- how long -- how long are the delays now? And how does that compare with what the delays were when this Act was passed?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Industry representatives",
      "case_id": "2018-17-571",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "1afaf600dd2608f30f4fcb02b7bdcc9d7e90a9175743ea9a42338f6558262211",
      "evidence_id": "ev-1afaf600dd26-0002-0005",
      "kind": "stated_consequence",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 45
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the rule adopted here would have a devastating impact and would cause severe hardship."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2018-17-571",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "1afaf600dd2608f30f4fcb02b7bdcc9d7e90a9175743ea9a42338f6558262211",
      "evidence_id": "ev-1afaf600dd26-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 48,
        "start": 48
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAVANAUGH: You -- you made an analogy to exhaustion of administrative remedies. I just want to test that --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2018-17-571",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "1afaf600dd2608f30f4fcb02b7bdcc9d7e90a9175743ea9a42338f6558262211",
      "evidence_id": "ev-1afaf600dd26-0002-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 49,
        "start": 49
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAVANAUGH: Well, is it -- is it even within the ZIP code?"
    },
